WEBVTT

00:04:57.363 --> 00:05:00.984
but the key point here, though,
is that we should think about loneliness

00:05:01.008 --> 00:05:03.613
as an important health threat,

00:05:03.637 --> 00:05:09.526
in the same way that we think about
obesity or smoking or sedentary living.

00:05:09.550 --> 00:05:12.850
AG: The social science on the health
effects is really nuanced here.

00:05:12.874 --> 00:05:15.366
Loneliness is only one
of the factors being measured,

00:05:15.390 --> 00:05:17.061
and we don't know that it's causal.

00:05:17.085 --> 00:05:19.913
But I was intrigued that this issue
caught Vivek's attention

00:05:19.937 --> 00:05:21.100
as a medical expert.

00:05:21.124 --> 00:05:24.155
VM: Once you become lonely,
you enter into this downward spiral,

00:05:24.179 --> 00:05:26.826
where you start to turn
further and further inward.

00:05:26.850 --> 00:05:31.643
You can actually become more difficult
to be around, in fact, for others,